BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 375.55 Tm (Firsthand Failure Modes, Traps & Economics Checks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 353.32 Tm (Enforcement is real but uneven, and the operators who have seen it are specific about the cost. Ryan Anthony warns) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 338.10 Tm (that Visa and Mastercard run secret shoppers. He calls it rare but says it happens, and the shoppers photograph receipts,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 322.87 Tm (menus, and invoices to check whether a pass-through program is compliant [KsqD8Ch93YI @ 00:01:00]. He says he) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 307.65 Tm (has personally seen merchants fined. The first fine is $1,000, another $5,000 is added if the problem is not fixed within) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 292.42 Tm (roughly 30 or 45 days, and the fines keep climbing from there. He has also heard secondhand of $25,000 fines per) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 277.20 Tm (incident [KsqD8Ch93YI @ 00:11:14]. On the Global Legal Law Firm podcast, the hosts confirm that secret shoppers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 261.97 Tm (are still out there issuing fines, though they hear of it less and less [rj9tjHr1nNo @ 00:11:14]. The firm also describes a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 246.75 Tm (legal dead end. It tried to sue Visa over the fines as unfair and anti-competitive, and the suit did not work. Visa says it) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 231.52 Tm (is not fining the ISO; it is fining the bank. The bank passes the fine to the processor, the processor passes it to the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 216.30 Tm (merchant, and the bank, which is making money on the arrangement, will never sue [rj9tjHr1nNo @ 00:12:09]. Under) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 201.07 Tm (that chain, every penalty ends up with the merchant, and agents need to explain that before signing anyone onto a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 185.85 Tm (program.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 170.62 Tm (Most failed programs are surcharges under a different label. Anthony says the old non-cash adjustment fee is a no-no.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 155.40 Tm (Adding the adjustment and then discounting it back off for cash payers is what the card brands call an effective) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 140.17 Tm (surcharge, which puts the merchant back under the debit ban and the 3% cap [KsqD8Ch93YI @ 00:12:13]. POS Nexus) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 124.95 Tm (lists where dual pricing programs go wrong: only some prices get updated, the gap is a round 4% instead of the actual) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 109.72 Tm (cost, and nobody told the staff. It adds that posting the cash price and adding a card fee at the till is a surcharge,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 94.50 Tm (whatever the merchant calls it [ZAtYPaS2xkA @ 00:01:24]. James Huber, who litigates these issues for Global Legal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 79.27 Tm (Law Firm, flags California restaurants that put an inflation, service, or health-benefits fee of 4% to 7% at the bottom of) Tj ET
