BT /F2 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 755.00 Tm (THE BIG MONEY PLAYBOOKS) Tj ET
0.6 w 54.00 747.00 m 558.00 747.00 l S
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (the menu. He says the restaurant carve-out does not cover a customer who never saw the fee, so the right approach is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (two prices on every menu line [rj9tjHr1nNo @ 00:10:19]. Debit cards are the other common trap. WKYC reports that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (federal law makes surcharges illegal on debit transactions, even when the debit card is processed like a credit card) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (without a PIN [AGTRnXUImOw @ 00:00:51]. Any terminal that cannot tell the card types apart is a liability for the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (merchant.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (The economics checks are where agents and merchants get misled. CCSalesPro's James Shepherd walks through the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (offset math. A merchant doing $100,000 a month that adds a 3.99% card price grows to $103,990 in volume. To net out) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (the $3,990, the processor bills roughly 3.84%, not 3.99%, because the fees now also apply to the added volume) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm ([ZRmKamGyTPc @ 00:03:07]. He warns that some processors hide the trade-off entirely. Their minimalist statements) Tj ET
