BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (Where Practitioners Disagree & Alternative Playbooks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 693.77 Tm (The sharpest split is over how many alert networks to stack. Georges Rayess frames Ethoca and Verifi as two halves of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 678.55 Tm (one defense, Mastercard on one side and Visa on the other, and insists there is no overlap and no single product covers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 663.32 Tm (both networks, so running only one leaves the other brand's disputes uncovered [gH8-LQ4srZY @ 00:02:28]. Scott E.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 648.10 Tm (Adams draws the map less cleanly: CDRN is mostly Visa and Ethoca is mostly Mastercard, but both carry some) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 632.87 Tm (coverage on both networks and can handle Discover and Amex depending on how the merchant is set up) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 617.65 Tm ([gROmfVmEsYs @ 00:02:13]. Chargeflow turns that overlap into a cost leak, warning that enrolling in both can fire) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 602.42 Tm (double dispute alerts when a cardholder's bank sits in both networks, which means double fees, so the golden rule is a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 587.20 Tm (cost-benefit analysis before committing [sBnXe7LYFO8 @ 00:06:18]. Sequencing splits the field too. Rayess says that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 571.97 Tm (if engineering time is tight, start with Verifi RDR because it is configure once and then autonomous. Adams runs the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 556.75 Tm (opposite order for merchants hit with a monitoring-program notice: get CDRN and Ethoca live for quick coverage,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 541.52 Tm (because both can be running in about 24 hours, then get into RDR and go from there [gROmfVmEsYs @ 00:03:09].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 526.30 Tm (Nobody quotes the same price for an alert, and the spread changes the math. Chargeflow says both Verifi CDRN and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.07 Tm (Ethoca levy a uniform $40 charge for each alert received, regardless of its success, then pitches its own bundled layer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (as paying only for alerts that actually prevented a chargeback, with no duplicate charges [sBnXe7LYFO8 @ 00:06:00].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (Chargeback.io quotes $29 per Ethoca alert and a shared $15 rate for RDR and CDRN, billed only for alerts received,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.40 Tm (and needs nothing but a billing descriptor to enroll Ethoca and CDRN [sH9CslJpDeA @ 00:01:33]. Georges Rayess) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.17 Tm (pegs the intercept at roughly $5 to $15 per alert against a $15 to $25 chargeback fee, and argues the per-alert fee) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 434.95 Tm (matters less than the ratio, because an intercepted dispute never posts as a chargeback and never counts toward) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.72 Tm (Mastercard's ECM program or Visa's VAMP [gH8-LQ4srZY @ 00:01:34]. Pablo Torres remembers the older) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.50 Tm (resistance: merchants Torres talked to asked why they should pay $35 for an alert when they could just focus on not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 389.27 Tm (getting the chargeback at all, which Torres calls the right attitude [fO958wEcK8A @ 00:10:04]. Read side by side, the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 374.05 Tm (same alert ranges from $5 to $40 depending on the vendor quoting it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 358.82 Tm (The deepest philosophical fight is whether to refund on autopilot or keep eyes on every dispute. Adams pitches Ethoca) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 343.60 Tm (partly as a way to automate the chargeback process and just not worry about it, and suggests lower-ticket or higher-risk) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 328.37 Tm (merchants simply refund the SAFE fraud-feed alerts while higher-ticket or lower-risk merchants test and possibly skip) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 313.15 Tm (them [Ghanuu5dNMk @ 00:02:49]. Rayess flags the cost of autopilot: RDR auto-refunds disputes you might have won) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 297.92 Tm (in representment, so the rules have to be calibrated to your reason-code mix [gH8-LQ4srZY @ 00:01:53]. Pablo Torres) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 282.70 Tm (goes further, arguing Ethoca and Verifi should not be a fraud or chargeback mitigation strategy at all, only a short break) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 267.47 Tm (while the root issue gets fixed, and that asking a vendor to stop telling you about refunds is turning a blind eye) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 252.25 Tm ([fO958wEcK8A @ 00:10:31]. On the fight side, Adaptiv Payments says save representment for the disputes you can) Tj ET
